          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Math Talk 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.123,
            0.801,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can the product of a decimal and a natural number be a natural number?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.179,
            0.847,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The distance between Ajay's school and his home is 827 m. He walks to school in the morning and then walks back home in the evening, 6 days a week. How much does he walk in a week? Answer in kilometres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.26,
            0.846,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each way between school and home, Ajay walks 827 metres, i.e., 0.827 km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.299,
            0.388,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, in a day he walks,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.288,
            0.32,
            0.71,
            0.358
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "0.827 \\times 2 = \\frac{827}{1000} \\times 2 = \\frac{827 \\times 2}{1000} = \\frac{1654}{1000} = 1.654"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.36,
            0.718,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "He goes to school 6 days a week. So, in a week, he walks"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.283,
            0.381,
            0.716,
            0.418
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "1.654 \\times 6 = \\frac{1654}{1000} \\times 6 = \\frac{1654 \\times 6}{1000} = \\frac{9924}{1000} = 9.924"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.421,
            0.433,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ajay walks 9.924 km a week."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.454,
            0.546,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4:",
              "styles": [
